Here's the big problem with Nethack! I love this game, and could easily
play it a lot more than I do now. Trouble is, I know that every time I
start I may be occupied for the next 12 hours or so. What's the solution?
A smaller dungeon might help. I find the endless mazes the most boring
bit in the game - maybe they could go.

Aren't the maze levels just a relic from the old Hack anyway? What
useful purpose do they really serve? Why not just have the demon lord
levels, call it the "9 Planes of Hell" or something and make it a branch
dungeon like the mines, rather than something you have to traverse
with a wizard in tow? I would enjoy this game a lot more if it wasn't
for those mazes. We still need Gehennom (?), so that the gateway
exists, but that could easily exist under the wizard's levels. Maybe
two or three levels after the Wizard, then the gate.

